+def _venue_consistency(row, q1, q2, n1, n2, floor) -> Dict[str, Any]:
+    """★ E-0912-A (c) criterion (i), for ONE execution_of_unknown_size leg — RECORD ONLY (the anomaly still stands).
+    Self-consistent means: every SENT request of the row has a confirmed quantity that its own child fills determine
+    (Σ trade_qty == |confirmed_qty|, joined on the venue's orderId) and that does not exceed the request's capacity
+    (`qty_venue` — the venue's origQty when it clamped — else `qty`); and the readback quantity equals the previous
+    position + the row's known part within the dust floor. That is exactly the 12Z shape: origQty == Σ children ==
+    the position, readback 0 (E-0912-A ③). A leg whose known part does NOT explain the readback, whose children do not
+    add up, or whose row carries no known quantity is NOT self-consistent — the full response stays right for it."""
