+"""E-0912-A (c): a PROPORTIONAL response to a venue-consistent `execution_of_unknown_size` — behind a switch, DEFAULT OFF.
+
+*** MOCK ONLY: MockBroker, temp state dirs, a pilot_log tree built from the fixture rows. No venue, no credentials,
+    nothing written under state/. ***
+
+THE RULING THIS SUITE SERVES (DESIGN_reduce_only_clamp_identity_2026-09-12 §2c): on 2026-09-12 12:47Z two names whose
+executions were fully knowable from the venue's own records (1,524 USDT = 0.65% of gross) tripped §4-5b and §4-7 and the
+ladder flattened the WHOLE book (235,383 USDT, ≈245 USDT of cost). (a)+(b) remove the cause. (c) asks a different question:
+when the SAME shape recurs for another reason, is "flatten everything" the right response to a few names the venue can
+account for? That is a book-behaviour change ⇒ the user's call — RULED 2026-09-12 13:19Z (relayed by the lead): thorough fix,
+no rollback, option A as the DEFAULT. This commit implements option A behind `watchdog.UNKNOWN_SIZE_LOCAL_RESPONSE`
+(default True = the ruling; False = option C, the pre-ruling ladder for every unknown-size anomaly) with tests on both
+sides of it.
+
+FROZEN CRITERIA (reconcile.unknown_size_local_eligibility; thresholds reconcile.UNKNOWN_SIZE_LOCAL_MAX_FRAC 2% /
+UNKNOWN_SIZE_LOCAL_MAX_NAMES 5): every anomaly at the latest anchor is an execution_of_unknown_size whose venue records are
+self-consistent (`_venue_consistency`: child fills within the request capacity determine the confirmed quantity; readback
+== position + known part within the dust floor) AND names ≤ 5 AND Σ|intended| ≤ 2% of the anchor's target gross (no
+anchors row ⇒ not eligible). §4-5b and §4-7 read ONE partition under ONE switch.
+
+THE FIXTURE AFTER (1): (a)+(b)+(1) re-derive the REAL 12Z rows' persisted contradiction into a KNOWN quantity (the venue asked
+for LESS: origQty 1933692 < ours 1933986), so those rows no longer yield the anomaly (c) is about — T8.0 pins that. (c)'s
+subject is the SAME anomaly kind for another reason: here the real rows with the persisted string's venue number raised
+ABOVE ours (venue ×1.001 — "the venue asked for MORE than we sent", which (1) must not re-derive) while the venue's own
+records stay self-consistent (children == confirmed ≤ ours, readback == position + known part). Everything below runs on
+that re-shaped day (`ORD`); the pristine rows are `ORD_REAL`.
+
+T8 — asserted here, on the real 12Z rows re-shaped as above (tests_fixtures/e0912a_12z) laid out as a pilot_log day:
+  T8.0  the switch DEFAULTS to True (USER RULING 2026-09-12 13:19Z, option A); reconcile RECORDS eligibility either
+        way (2 names, 0.65%, eligible).
+  T8.A  switch False (option C, kept as a tested branch) ⇒ the pre-ruling behaviour byte for byte: §4-5b + §4-7 trigger,
+        tripped, the ladder runs, state carries `degradation`; the eligibility is visible in the 5b detail as "would have
+        been local".
+  T8.B  switch True (the default) ⇒ NOT tripped, no trigger, `local_responses` names both; halt_opening_orders YES, flatten_all NO,
+        reduce-only key NOT set; 5b state LOCAL; §4-7 drift False from the SAME partition; state.json kind
+        local_response with tripped_at (the anchor re-applies the opening halt) and open_orders_halted; ALARM.log HIGH;
+        events.jsonl row flagged local_response; the re-check saw both names flat.
+  T8.C  switch True, 6 names ⇒ not eligible (names) ⇒ full ladder.       T8.D  switch True, 3% of gross ⇒ full ladder.
+  T8.E  switch True, NOT self-consistent (readback ≠ position + known; child fills ≠ confirmed) ⇒ full ladder.
+  T8.F  switch True, eligible, but the venue re-read shows a name still holding: below dust ⇒ recorded, no order;
+        above dust ⇒ THAT name only is flattened reduce-only by the unexplained part, rows + readback written.
+  T8.G  switch True, a quantity_residual anomaly beside the unknown-size ones ⇒ full ladder;  no anchors row ⇒ full ladder.
+  T8.H  a trip outranks a local response: with the switch on, an unrelated trigger still runs the ladder.
+
