submit record is bound by the client id WE sent (a response naming another id lends no orderId and fails the present-field gate). Round 12 (review 83fcbbcc, DESIGN §3f / §5 field-by-reader table): that the submit response's direct reader checks the body against the order we sent before reading a number (a body naming another client id is a contradiction, and no re-query is made under that id), that a merged record whose quantity 0 is a LOWER BOUND is compatible with a positive final amount (NEW 0 → fills → cancel with an amount-only terminal read ⇒ known 0 / band 10 / amount 4, total [6, 16] beside a top-up of 6) while a raw same-snapshot 0-beside-amount stays a contradiction, that a final amount is constant against child fills and a subset's amount may not exceed it, that a duplicate trade id without a quote never erases a recorded quote, that a child subset's vwap goes to its own column and never becomes the row's price, that an amount known beside an unknown quantity is the interval [0, Q] (known 0 + band, on the UNKNOWN row and the normal maker ledger alike — a contract choice registered in DESIGN §3f.6), and that explicit zeros carry the amount's finality. Round 13 (review ec2fe835, DESIGN §3g): that the child-fill amount LOWER BOUND (Σ over the children that carry a quote) is compared against a final amount without waiting for the others (5/N50 + 5/N-missing against a final 40 is a contradiction), that a non-finite ledger amount is flagged even when the quantity is missing, that every identity gate reads a present-but-malformed field (empty side, non-finite origQty) as a contradiction and an absent one as no evidence (one `identity_field` for the submit gate, the re-query gate and the settlement's present-field gate), and that the two cost diagnostics (neutrality_price, chase_readout.collect) measure bps over PRICED fills only and report the unpriced count / notional / fee beside it (no priced fill ⇒ None, never 0). Round 14 (review d51cb731): that an order id